// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel
// Note: DeviceAlertEvents is NOT available in Microsoft Sentinel Log Analytics — it
// is a Defender XDR Advanced Hunting-only table, even with the Microsoft Defender
// XDR connector enabled (see docs/reference/sentinel-vs-advanced-hunting.md, Section
// 2/3). This file is kept for structural parity with kql/xdr/identity/ and as a
// reference for what the equivalent Sentinel query would look like if Microsoft
// ever exposes this table — it will not return results, and will error with
// "table not found", in a real Sentinel workspace today. Use Sentinel's own
// SecurityAlert / SecurityIncident tables for device-scoped alert history instead.
// Identity / triage — all Defender alerts for a specific device
// Use at the start of any investigation to get the full picture before drilling into logs
// Replace HOSTNAME before running
// Ref: docs/scenarios/01-malware-alert/investigation.md

let target_device = "HOSTNAME";   // replace before running
let lookback = 7d;
DeviceAlertEvents
| where DeviceName == target_device
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| project TimeGenerated, AlertId, Title, Severity
| order by TimeGenerated desc

